 r←SelectHelp(mustFlag quitFlag allFlag maxSel)
⍝ Returns the lines `Select` puts on display when the user enters a "?".\\
⍝ Only what this particular call allows is mentioned, so the flags decide what the user gets to see.\\
⍝ Note that "∘∘∘" is deliberately not mentioned: that's for programmers, see the documentation.
 r←''
 :If 1=maxSel
     r,←⊂'Enter the number of the item you want to select'
 :Else
     r,←⊂'Enter the number of the item you want to select, or several of them, separated by spaces or commas'
     r,←⊂'A range like "3-6" stands for the items 3, 4, 5 and 6'
 :EndIf
 :If allFlag
     r,←⊂'Enter "a" for all items, or "a~3 5" for all items but 3 and 5'
     :If 1<maxSel
         r,←⊂'A range may follow "a~" as well: "a~3-5" selects all items but 3, 4 and 5'
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
 :If quitFlag
     r,←⊂'Enter "q" in order to quit without selecting anything'
 :EndIf
 :If ~mustFlag
     r,←⊂'Press <enter> without entering anything in order to select nothing'
 :EndIf
 r←('  * '∘,)¨r
⍝Done
